  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -334,9 +334,9 @@ The following file formats can be saved by Wireshark (with the known file extens\n \n * EyeSDN USB S0 traces ({asterisk}.trc)\n \n-* Textronix K12 text file format captures ({asterisk}.txt)\n+* Tekronix K12 text file format captures ({asterisk}.txt)\n \n-* Textronix K12xx 32bit .rf5 format captures ({asterisk}.rf5)\n+* Tektronix K12xx 32bit .rf5 format captures ({asterisk}.rf5)\n \n * Android Logcat binary logs ({asterisk}.logcat)\n \n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "docbook/wsug_src/WSUG_chapter_io.adoc",
      "old_path": "docbook/wsug_src/WSUG_chapter_io.adoc",
      "a_mode": "100644",
      "b_mode": "100644",
      "new_file": false,
      "renamed_file": false,
      "deleted_file": false,
      "generated_file": null
    },
    {
      "diff": "@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@ The following features are new (or have been significantly updated) since versio\n * Wireshark now supports dissecting the rtp packet with OPUS payload.\n \n * Importing captures from text files is now also possible based on regular expressions. By specifying a regex capturing a single\n-  packet including capturing groups for relevant fields a textfile can be converted to a libcap capture file. Supported data\n+  packet including capturing groups for relevant fields a textfile can be converted to a libpcap capture file. Supported data\n   encodings are plain-hexadecimal, -octal, -binary and base64.\n   Also the timestamp format now allows the second-fractions to be placed anywhere in the timestamp and it will be stored with\n   nanosecond instead of microsecond precision.\n@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@ The following features are new (or have been significantly updated) since versio\n ** RTP Player added to menu Telephony>RTP>RTP Player\n \n * VoIP dialogs (VoIP Calls, RTP Streams, RTP Analysis, RTP Player, SIP Flows) are non-modal, can stay opened on background\n-** Same tools are provided acros all dialogs (Prepare Filter, Analyse, RTP Player ...)\n+** Same tools are provided across all dialogs (Prepare Filter, Analyse, RTP Player ...)\n \n * Follow stream is now able to follow SIP call by SIP.Call-ID\n \n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "docbook/release-notes.adoc",
      "old_path": "docbook/release-notes.adoc",
